infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title Run it on seam signals, not green dashboards
  desc Every per-service dashboard can stay green while the pipeline quietly fails customers — these four signals live between layers
  lists
    - label Consumer lag
      desc How far behind the saga's event consumers are. Rising lag means the pipeline is falling behind producers; sagas stall mid-flight and in-flight compensations pile up.
    - label Quorum write/read latency
      desc p99 of the W=2 write. A slow third replica drags tail latency even when no node is technically down.
    - label Leader churn
      desc Elections per minute. Frequent re-elections mean fencing tokens are bumping constantly — you are one pause away from a split-brain write attempt.
    - label Retry-budget exhaustion
      desc Percent of budget consumed. Near 100%, retries get dropped and surface as user-visible failures even though every downstream service is healthy. Budgets cap retries at ~10% over normal request rate.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
